# Compiled binary (go build -o nexusgate ./cmd/nexusgate)
/nexusgate

# Local Hub data directory: SQLite, cache, admin-token, agent-token,
# provider-secrets. Never commit — it holds the Hub credentials and the
# encrypted provider keys. NEXUSGATE_DATA_DIR can point anywhere, so the
# credential filenames are also matched on their own below.
.nexusgate-dev/
.nexusgate*/

# Hub credentials by name, wherever a data directory ends up. These are
# generated at first start and are the whole authorization boundary; the store
# key decrypts every provider secret.
admin-token
agent-token
provider-secrets/
store.key

# Real configuration. config.example.json is the tracked template.
config.json

# Compose reads .env automatically, and docker-compose.yml passes six provider
# key variables through from it. That makes an untracked .env the intended place
# for them and a tracked one a committed key. No .env.example is shipped — the
# documented template is config.example.json (and the README's Configuration
# section), which carries no key values. The negation below only guards a
# value-free .env.example if one is ever added.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Real MCP configuration carries agent/admin tokens. The tracked template is
# skills/nexusgate/mcp/.mcp.json.example; a filled-in copy at the repo root or
# anywhere else must never be committed.
.mcp.json
# The Claude Code plugin's declaration (plugins/claude/.mcp.json) is a
# token-free template — stdio command plus ${VAR} env passthrough, never a
# secret — so it is committed despite the general rule above.
!plugins/claude/.mcp.json

# Editor/backup noise.
*.tmp
*.bak
*~

# Worker configuration written by `nexusgate worker enroll` (node token).
worker.json

*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Go test binaries (go test -c) and coverage output.
*.test
coverage.out
*.cover

# Media fixtures produced by hand while testing the pipeline. Source footage is
# never stored in the repo, and internal/media's integration test generates
# whatever it needs at run time.
/testdata-local/

# macOS directory metadata.
.DS_Store

# Server logs from a hand-run `nexusgate serve` during testing.
*.log
*.tar.gz

# Stray build artifacts from local packaging. The MCP server builds from
# cmd/nexusgate-mcp; a committed binary only bloats history. Anchored with a
# leading slash like /nexusgate above, and for the same reason: unanchored,
# "nexusgate-mcp" matches the cmd/nexusgate-mcp *directory* too, which made
# every new file added there invisible to git status and git add. Already
# tracked files kept working, so the masking only ever bit new ones.
/nexusgate-mcp
/nexusgate-corpusgen
/dist/

# Playwright CLI session artifacts.
.playwright-cli/

# Local demo screenshots.
demo-*.png

# Deterministic on-disk SQLite scale benchmark databases and WAL sidecars.
.bench/sqlite/

# Repository-local Go module, build, and temporary caches used by constrained CI/dev hosts.
.cache/

# Personal working notes: these tracked host addresses and a TLS fingerprint
# until the v0.31 audit found them in pushed history. They stay local.
state.md
v021-unreleased-state.md

# Agent worktrees and local Claude state — never part of the published tree.
.claude/
